# Welcome to EHttpEditor!
#
# This file holds HTTP requests. Each request starts with a line "###" (followed by an optional name), then:
#   - the request line: the method (GET when it is left out) and the URL;
#   - the headers, one "Name: value" a line;
#   - an empty line, then the body (for POST, PUT, PATCH...).
#
# To run a request, click "Send request" above it, or put the cursor in it and press Ctrl+Enter
# (Ctrl+Shift+Enter runs all the requests of the file). The response shows in the HTTP Client view below:
# body, headers, the request sent, the results of the tests and the console of the scripts.
#
# Lines starting with # or // are comments. The guide: Help > Documentation.

# A variable: "@name = value", used as {{name}} in the requests below it.
@host = https://httpbin.org

### A simple GET
# The query parameters can be written on several lines, starting with ? and &: they are encoded for you.
# {{$uuid}} is a dynamic variable: a new random value each time the request runs.
GET {{host}}/get
    ?search=eclipse http
    &id={{$uuid}}
Accept: application/json

### A POST with a JSON body and a test
# The body comes after the empty line. {{$isoTimestamp}} is the current date and time.
POST {{host}}/post
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "EHttpEditor",
  "time": "{{$isoTimestamp}}"
}

# A response handler: JavaScript run after the response is received. client.test adds a test to the Tests tab,
# and client.global.set keeps a value for the next requests, as {{name}}.
> {%
client.test("The request succeeded", function () {
  client.assert(response.status === 200, "Response status is not 200");
});
client.global.set("name", response.body.json.name);
%}

### Uses the value kept by the previous request (run the POST first)
GET {{host}}/anything/{{name}}

### A request with the variables of an environment
# The environments are in http-client.env.json, next to this file: Environments > Edit Environments creates it with
# examples. The secrets (passwords, tokens) go in http-client.private.env.json (Environments > Edit Private
# Environments), a file which is not shared. Choose the environment with Environments > Select Environment
# (Ctrl+Alt+E), or with "Environment:" above the first request of the file.
# With the environment "dev" of the examples, {{baseUrl}} is https://httpbin.org (from "$shared", in every
# environment), {{user}} is "dev" and {{password}} is "dev-secret". Hover a variable to see its value.
# "Authorization: Basic user password" is encoded for you.
GET {{baseUrl}}/basic-auth/{{user}}/{{password}}
Authorization: Basic {{user}} {{password}}
